WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.261
DNS identity, the authoritative mapping
of names to addresses and owners,

2
00:00:05.261 --> 00:00:07.738
is the first link in the trust chain.

3
00:00:07.738 --> 00:00:11.410
Certificates, policies
and tokens all name their

4
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.262
subject by FQDN and trust
DNS to get the caller there.

5
00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:20.113
Moving to Entra ID tokens removes the
domain controller but adds names that must

6
00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:24.674
resolve consistently, like the right
sign-in endpoint for the cloud you're in.

7
00:00:24.674 --> 00:00:27.991
Here's the certificate
version of split-brain:

8
00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:33.663
a CA's revocation names exist only in AD
DNS, and a cloud caller can't resolve them.

9
00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:37.789
One client breaks the handshake,
another quietly skips the check,

10
00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:41.075
nothing is logged, and the
ticket goes to the PKI team.

11
00:00:41.075 --> 00:00:42.488
That's Decision 5.

12
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:46.211
And for regional naming,
certificate wildcards are narrow,

13
00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:48.240
so use per-region names instead.
